new-page: true

= The Last Majles

## Iran, 1949–1953

You represent the coordinating leadership of the National Front. Build an
effective constitutional opposition, hold together a diverse coalition, and
prepare for the struggle over representative government and Iranian control of
the oil industry.

- @start_game: Start game
- @about: About this prototype

@start_game
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.started = 1;

// Calendar: October 1949. As in SPD, one normal action advances one month.
Q.time = 1;
Q.year = 1949;
Q.month = 10;
Q.month_actions = 0;

// Coalition resources. These are prototype balance values, not historical data.
Q.resources = 2;
Q.dues = 3;
Q.coalition_cohesion = 50;
Q.constitutional_legitimacy = 50;
Q.public_mandate = 35;
Q.organizational_reach = 20;
Q.political_intelligence = 20;

// Named relationships remain numerical during the SPD-baseline phase.
Q.mossadegh_authority = 60;
Q.iran_party_relation = 55;
Q.toilers_relation = 40;
Q.muslim_warriors_relation = 35;
Q.court_relation = 15;

// Card cooldowns.
Q.coalition_meeting_timer = 0;
Q.press_coordination_timer = 0;
Q.electoral_committee_timer = 0;
Q.timers = [
    'coalition_meeting',
    'press_coordination',
    'electoral_committee'
];
!}
go-to: palace_protest

@about
new-page: true

= About this prototype

This build establishes the same basic implementation rhythm as *Dynamic Social
Democracy*: initialize a large shared state, draw organizational action cards,
take one strategic action per month, update the simulation, and resolve events.

The historical campaign is not implemented yet. Numerical effects in this build
are tuning placeholders rather than estimates of historical quantities.

- @start_menu: Return to title
